  "comment": "About 160 species of the Pacific Northwest's lowlands, Seattle to Portland and Eugene: the 150 bird species with the most research-grade iNaturalist observations created up to 2026-11-09 across ten Washington counties (Skagit, Island, Snohomish, King, Kitsap, Pierce, Thurston, Lewis, Cowlitz, Clark) and ten Oregon counties (Columbia, Multnomah, Washington, Clackamas, Yamhill, Marion, Polk, Benton, Linn, Lane), minus the domestic Muscovy Duck, plus ten heard more than seen (Marsh Wren, Western Flycatcher, Hutton's and Warbling Vireos, Black-throated Grey Warbler, Willow and Olive-sided Flycatchers, Western Screech Owl, Mountain Pygmy Owl, Red Crossbill). iNaturalist splits the Marsh Wren and BirdNET does not: the entry keeps BirdNET's Cistothorus palustris with iNaturalist's Western Marsh Wren (taxon 1721810), the one that lives here. `packbuilder draft --place 1236 --place 2998 --place 410 --place 1282 --place 1231 --place 411 --place 1666 --place 2742 --place 517 --place 502 --place 1848 --place 984 --place 540 --place 536 --place 558 --place 538 --place 485 --place 484 --place 535 --place 981 --before 2026-11-09 --top 150 --exclude 'Cairina moschata' --add ...`. scientific_name and common_name follow the BirdNET+ label file as in us-ca-la (species the committed packs already list reuse their entries); inat_taxon_id is iNaturalist's; wikipedia_url is iNaturalist's link for the taxon. The order is the observation ranking, then the species added by hand. Drafted with `packbuilder draft` and read over by a person; tests/test_definition.py checks the labels.",
